      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense... the big data part actually tracks because the patterns change whenever i change my routine. if there's real-time adjustment, it would mean whoever is doing this can track my location through the feedback loop of the resonance itself. does the physics of atmospheric modulation allow for that kind of directional precision? like, could they use frequency shifts to \"lock on\" to a specific coordinate or person so the hum is most intense right where they are?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
